<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=irrigation">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Farming and food</p><h1 class="enc-title">Irrigation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 6000 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Irrigation is the practice of applying controlled amounts of water to land to help grow crops, with some of the earliest known use dating to the 6th millennium BCE in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzistan</a>, south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. Choga Mami in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> is believed to show the first canal irrigation, at about 6000 BCE; the earliest known canals in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>'s Zaña Valley, date to at least 3400 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egyptians">Egyptians</a> let the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> flood into basins enclosed by dykes, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s Dujiangyan system, built in 256 BCE, still supplies water.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/irrigation.jpg" alt="Irrigation" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photography: Barbara Steinemann; derivative work by Zacharie Grossen · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bisse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 6000 BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Khuzistan (Iran) and Choga Mami (Iraq)</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Also arose independently</span>Zaña Valley, Peru (by 3400 BCE)</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/neolithic-revolution">Agriculture<span>c. 10,000 BCE</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/anden">Andean terraces<span>by 2000 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/stepwell">Stepwell<span>2650–1450 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/aqueduct">Aqueduct<span>c. 2000 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/qanat">Qanat<span>c. 1000 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/grand-canal">Grand Canal<span>486 BCE–609 CE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/water-wheel">Water wheel<span>4th century BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/chinampa">Chinampa<span>c. 1150</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=irrigation">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
